\ An `inline` word whose body raises, for inline_error_frames_crossmod.1z to import.
\
\ Its body reaches only natives, so the relocation rule lets the copy cross into the importing
\ module. The copied instructions keep line 9, which is a line in this file and not in the one
\ they end up in.
\
\ The raise sits inside a quotation rather than at the body's top level, because a quotation is
\ its own instruction array with no runs recorded over it. Reaching this word's name from in
\ there is what says the walk leaves the quotation and reads the run around the call that
\ entered it.

\\ Write a value to a stream, and drop the count.
write-it: ( s v -- ) const inline [ [ stream-write ] call drop ] ;
